      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Good race but ZOURATA (2) looks well placed to break through. Was a winner five back then has placed 3/4 since, the latest just missing here at the same trip. Has raced six times this course and distance for four wins and a placing and will take catching again. ANSON BAY (8) is in great form, the latest scoring by a space here over 1300m. Comes back in trip and this is harder but significant weight drop and looks tough to stop again. FIELD OF FLUTES (1) is another racing in great heart, winning two on end before finishing runner-up latest. Hard to fault form and will take catching again. SHIRSHOV (4) wasn't far away fresh and strips fitter. LIM'S IDA (7) is a former Victorian who has been racing in town in Melbourne and could easily measure up in this class.",
